    "The anchor redeemed WETH, which needed the gateway's WETH listing (erc20s mapping) set by a governance request after the host was pointed at HandlerV1; as a listing the exploit needed it is the latest reset (rule 8).",
    "Loss is a floor: escrow and host-fee outflows in forged requests, plus what pre-existing bridged-DOT pools paid out before each pool's first liquidity change. MANTA and CERE are at the attacker's sale proceeds, far below market. Later pool outflows, dilution and DOT-denominated losses are excluded.",
    "Campaign: every successful handlePostRequests with a leaf index at or above leafCount on the six chains running HandlerV1. Earlier calls were checked for relayers seen five times or fewer; none were forged. DOT mint-and-dump txs using the hijacked admin count in the loss but are not listed."
